  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience is individuals familiar with absurdist humor and satire, particularly those who recognize the meme format of juxtaposing a serious-looking official (often a politician or bureaucrat) with an absurd, impossible scenario. The meme relies on cultural references to Dante Alighieri and 'Dante's Inferno' to create humor through illogical juxtaposition. The intended audience likely includes internet users who appreciate political satire and are aware of the trope of mocking bureaucratic incompetence through absurdity. The black-and-white office setting and the man’s formal attire serve as visual cues that signal the target audience to interpret the image as a satirical commentary on authority figures, making it most effective for those who understand and engage with this form of absurdist political humor.",
